Package: nvim-forge
Version: 1.0.0
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6
Maintainer: nvim-forge Maintainers <nvim-forge@localhost>
Description: Self-contained Neovim distribution with LSP for Python, C, C++ and Rust
 nvim-forge bundles everything needed for a modern Neovim programming
 environment into a single package: the Neovim editor itself, a curated
 plugin set, pre-built Tree-sitter parsers, the BasedPyright (Python),
 clangd (C/C++) and rust-analyzer (Rust) language servers, plus the
 runtimes they need (a Node.js runtime and a complete Rust toolchain
 including cargo, rustc, rust-std and rust-src).
 .
 After installation the editor works fully offline: no plugin manager
 bootstrap, no :TSInstall, no npm, no rustup, no Internet access of any
 kind is required.  The system Neovim is never touched; nvim-forge is
 launched with its own command and keeps all writable state in per-user
 XDG directories.
 .
 Launch with: nvim-forge
